  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The official OpenAI post announcing GPT-4 is from March 14, 2023:\n\n1. **@OpenAI** (Mar 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC) — “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4”  \n   https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185  \n   (~59.7k likes, ~16k reposts; includes video)\n\nRelated public posts from OpenAI leadership the same day:\n\n2. **@gdb (Greg Brockman)** — “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model (image & text in, text out)… passes many qualification benchmarks like the bar exam & AP Calculus”  \n   https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426\n\n3. **@sama (Sam Altman)** — “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet. it is available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.” (thread)  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393\n\n4. **@miramurati (Mira Murati)** — “Unveiling GPT-4 -- our large multimodal model that exhibits human-level performance on various professional and academic benchmarks…”  \n   https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121\n\n5. **@npew (Peter Welinder)** — “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet! Try it today on ChatGPT or join the API waitlist.”  \n   https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024\n\nCoverage of the announcement:\n\n6. **@verge** — “OpenAI announces GPT-4 — the next generation of its AI language model” linking The Verge story  \n   https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307\n\n7. The Verge article (Mar 14, 2023) — OpenAI announces GPT-4, text/image inputs, ChatGPT Plus and API waitlist  \n   https://www.theverge.com/2023/3/14/23638033/openai-gpt-4-chatgpt-multimodal-deep-learning\n\n8. OpenAI YouTube — “Introducing GPT-4” (published Mar 14–15, 2023), product page https://openai.com/product/gpt-4  \n   https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TxkJMX0KyS0",
